nverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the domain of $f(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-6<x<3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n-6<{f}^{-1}(x)<3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186561037 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8f4acd94-b4a7-59ce-b6cb-3d3310b167fd" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Domain and Range of an Inverse Function Using a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26720517-4d72-5460-b56e-b19365511cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560449} {:answer/id #uuid "a360d025-c375-5503-9d95-becd0af97805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\le {f}^{-1}(x)\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560697} {:answer/id #uuid "bf83acff-61f2-538c-8a3c-3655ca48cc76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560745} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5cc71d-222e-5763-9153-94ad33d3fa3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1\\le {f}^{-1}(x)\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560772} {:answer/id #uuid "ccbb1c10-5851-56e1-8bd3-1e66ddc4a54f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26720517-4d72-5460-b56e-b19365511cf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560449} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd345aa7-7bbc-5fb0-a28b-bbb1afa1e0e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560947}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a80e40f5-874e-56ab-80fe-9d43a174a171" :question/math-academy-id "q-7027" :question/problem "The domain of the function $f(x)$ is $x\\ge 4$ and the range of $f$ is $f(x)\\ge 2.$ What is the range of the inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the following:\n\n- The domain of a function $f(x)$ is the range of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\n- The range of a function $f(x)$ is the domain of its inverse function ${f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nThe domain of $f(x)$ is:\n\n$$\nx\\ge 4\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range of ${f}^{-1}(x)$ is:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)\\ge 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180264 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179757 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f9429da-a9d4-5dfc-940a-ef24066a5b65" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Range of an Inverse Function Using a Graph"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb74d47-5819-51e6-987f-c47594800e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560398} {:answer/id #uuid "84c08631-0c69-50aa-ad0b-25457d685152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560642} {:answer/id #uuid "93dd0e20-404e-5267-89e3-a04adfa86c34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5<{f}^{-1}(x)<-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560669} {:answer/id #uuid "b1e34b36-ae62-52f5-986a-3b72e39715be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5<{f}^{-1}(x)<-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560721} {:answer/id #uuid "ee173d36-05ed-5aa9-963b-321b4dde6642" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5<{f}^{-1}(x)<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0eb74d47-5819-51e6-987f-c47594800e7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/r